s lifetime**. Each such failed open leaks one JDK connection, and `dao.jing.remote` has no handle through which to prevent it. This is the shipped transport's behaviour and this plan does not change it (§8) | `[T→D]` — `network-invalid-url-test` pins only validation (§5.2 #5); §5.2 #5 and #6 pin the throw and that nothing escapes; nothing pins teardown, because there is none |\ndocs/design/dao.jing.remote.implementation-plan.md:358:socket exists, that seam records `:close-request` (`jvm.clj:168-173`) and\ndocs/design/dao.jing.remote.implementation-plan.md:696:165370 assertions / 0 failures 0 errors**, which includes\ndocs/design/dao.jing.remote.implementation-plan.md:700:dropping the once-only claim → 4 failures; chaining after failure → 1;\ndocs/design/dao.jing.remote.implementation-plan.md:1076:    `:close-request` and returns (`jvm.clj:168-173`); the pending\ndocs/design/dao.jing.cbor.md:520:These failures remain loud remote errors or explicit DHT refusal; there is\ndocs/design/dao.jing.cbor.md:678:- File reopen, duplicate insertion, durability failures, torn tails,\ndocs/design/dao.stream.file.md:373:  hide write failures indefinitely. The read is non-blocking.\ntest/yin/vm/ucf/authority/front_test.cljc:595:;; Gate follow-ups: carriage answers, reply failures, silent admissions\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.cursor-cell-numbering.md:373:Every refusal was (ii) or (iii); none was (i). Invariance failures and\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.cursor-cell-numbering.md:374:decode failures: 0 of 3300. The fourth review's independent 5,000-state\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.cursor-cell-numbering.md:798:stop at 6a's retained recompute budget, 0 other decode failures.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.cursor-cell-numbering.md:853:numbered, 0 invariance failures, 0 decode failures, at most 13 trials\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/waitset.cljc:217:  transport-error are terminal append failures under their own keywords —\ndocs/blogs-todo.md:83:- Handling partial failures and network partitions d